OL,3,AHeart, hope and a steely determination:
OL,4,ADolly Parton's musical legacy
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn 1980, Dolly Parton was filming her
OL,7,Ffirst Hollywood movie, 9 To 5, and
OL,8,Fbetween scenes she had an idea for the
OL,9,Ftune that would become the movie's
OL,10,Ftheme song.
OL,12,FBut her guitar was banned from the set
OL,13,F- so she made the beat by strumming her
OL,14,Facrylic nails together.
OL,16,FThe sound, she realised, was just like
OL,17,Fthe typewriter used by her character, a
OL,18,Fmarried secretary who is constantly
OL,19,Fbelittled and sexually harassed by her
OL,20,Fboss.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/39
